## Why

Parent: `folio-assistant-95e7`. cat-harness-tools `scripts/install-skills.ts --host copilot|claude` already writes `<host dir>/<prefix>-<name>/SKILL.md` with `INSTALLED_MARKER` and has `--check` for drift (bean `cat-tools-0nxe`). Nothing stops a hand-written file appearing beside them, which is how `.github/skills/` became a code library.

Blocked on bean `folio-assistant-hhkw` (the hand-written files must be gone first).

## Done when

- [ ] smart-base runs `install-skills --host copilot` and `--host claude`; `--check` runs in PR CI.
- [ ] A gate (cat-harness-tools, so every layer gets it) fails when a file under a host skill directory lacks the installed marker.
- [ ] A gate fails when a workflow `run:` invokes a path under `.github/` other than `.github/workflows/` or a declared directory.
- [ ] The `SGAuthoring.Skills.*` Requirements and `input/pagecontent/authoring-skills.md` link to the KG tool pages, not to `.github` paths.
